<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The chair is one of the most important and widely used pieces of furniture, serving both functional and aesthetic purposes. In ancient times, chairs were symbols of power and status, used mainly by royalty and elite classes. Over time, their use became more common, and the focus shifted towards comfort, usability, and design. Today, chairs are not only essential for seating but also play a key role in enhancing the visual appeal of a space.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Chairs are designed in different types based on their function, such as office chairs for work, study chairs for reading, dining chairs for meals, and lounge chairs for relaxation. Among these, the accent chair stands out as a statement piece that adds character and style to interiors while still being functional.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
